WEBVTT

1
00:52:19.786 --> 00:52:26.786
Thank you very much, Bent, for leading us to honor God.

2
00:52:26.786 --> 00:52:30.786
I loved it. I enjoyed it.

3
00:52:30.786 --> 00:52:33.786
But that is actually something God always does.

4
00:52:33.786 --> 00:52:39.786
When you open yourself up, He comes to meet you and draws closer.

5
00:52:39.786 --> 00:52:45.786
I must say, it is always a bit exciting to stand here on the podium.

6
00:52:45.786 --> 00:52:50.786
Maybe some people are used to it, but I still hear from others who also speak,

7
00:52:50.786 --> 00:52:55.786
that there are always some butterflies in the stomach before you go up.

8
00:52:55.786 --> 00:52:59.786
And then that somehow disappears.

9
00:52:59.786 --> 00:53:05.786
But the reason I want to stand here is because I want to bring something to you.

10
00:53:05.786 --> 00:53:11.786
Because I want to tell you about who God is and what He does.

11
00:53:11.786 --> 00:53:15.786
And I am actually honored and happy to share the Word with you.

12
00:53:15.786 --> 00:53:20.786
And that is actually the intention from which I start.

13
00:53:20.786 --> 00:53:29.786
And that has to do with, and why I can do that, has to do with the love that God has for me.

14
00:53:29.786 --> 00:53:32.786
And that I want to share. And that is what I will talk about today.

15
00:53:32.786 --> 00:53:35.786
The theme is God provides.

16
00:53:35.786 --> 00:53:39.786
And I want to talk today about how God provides in His love.

17
00:53:39.786 --> 00:53:46.786
But before we move on to the program, I had written about the church app.

18
00:53:46.786 --> 00:53:52.786
Because when I was preparing, I know that this is a bit of a deviation from myself.

19
00:53:52.786 --> 00:53:56.786
But I keep looking at who is in that church app.

20
00:53:56.786 --> 00:53:59.786
Which people are behind those names.

21
00:53:59.786 --> 00:54:04.786
And then I see people who just put their own photo on it.

22
00:54:04.786 --> 00:54:06.786
And that makes it easier to recognize then.

23
00:54:06.786 --> 00:54:09.786
There are some who put images on it.

24
00:54:09.786 --> 00:54:13.786
I'm not going to say anything, because then someone will feel addressed.

25
00:54:13.786 --> 00:54:15.786
But then I think, who could that be?

26
00:54:15.786 --> 00:54:20.786
So today a call, for the sake of clarity not arranged with Tim and Vanessa.

27
00:54:20.786 --> 00:54:23.786
A call to put an image behind it.

28
00:54:23.786 --> 00:54:27.786
Do you know how powerful that can be when you are at home, for example?

29
00:54:27.786 --> 00:54:29.786
And you are praying for the church.

30
00:54:29.786 --> 00:54:33.786
And you go through those faces.

31
00:54:34.786 --> 00:54:36.786
I have said, it is a deviation.

32
00:54:36.786 --> 00:54:39.786
I really enjoy looking at who is with us in the church.

33
00:54:39.786 --> 00:54:44.786
We are a large church and there is a danger that we have some distance from each other.

34
00:54:44.786 --> 00:54:47.786
And it can certainly never be that we are all friends with each other.

35
00:54:47.786 --> 00:54:50.786
That's not what I'm about, but we are connected to each other.

36
00:54:50.786 --> 00:54:54.786
And then it's nice to attach a face, or to attach a name.

37
00:54:54.786 --> 00:54:56.786
Because I see faces, I see a lot of faces now.

38
00:54:56.786 --> 00:54:58.786
But to attach a name to that face.

39
00:54:58.786 --> 00:55:00.786
So that you can also actively pray for someone.

40
00:55:00.786 --> 00:55:05.786
If we receive a message via WhatsApp that person needs help.

41
00:55:05.786 --> 00:55:07.786
Then you can know for whom you are praying.

42
00:55:07.786 --> 00:55:09.786
Shall we agree on that then?

43
00:55:09.786 --> 00:55:12.786
Putting a face on that church app.

44
00:55:13.786 --> 00:55:15.786
That was the announcement.

45
00:55:17.786 --> 00:55:24.786
So I want to start with a text that says something about what love is from the Biblical perspective.

46
00:55:24.786 --> 00:55:28.786
And very standard, we will actually go to 1 Corinthians 13.

47
00:55:28.786 --> 00:55:31.786
I want to read from verses 4 to 8.

48
00:55:32.786 --> 00:55:33.786
I will do that.

49
00:55:33.786 --> 00:55:36.786
Love is patient and kind.

50
00:55:36.786 --> 00:55:38.786
Love is not jealous.

51
00:55:38.786 --> 00:55:43.786
Love does not boast and does not think of itself as very important.

52
00:55:44.786 --> 00:55:50.786
Love does not say or do unkind things and does not think only of itself.

53
00:55:50.786 --> 00:55:53.786
Love is not bitter.

54
00:55:53.786 --> 00:55:56.786
Love forgives when someone has done something wrong.

55
00:55:57.786 --> 00:56:01.786
Love does not rejoice in dishonest things, but in the truth.

56
00:56:01.786 --> 00:56:05.786
Love does not gossip about the mistakes of others.

57
00:56:05.786 --> 00:56:09.786
Always think the best of another and always remain patient.

58
00:56:09.786 --> 00:56:15.786
Love never fails and never disappears.

59
00:56:16.786 --> 00:56:17.786
Good.

60
00:56:19.786 --> 00:56:22.786
I could speak about that, but I will not do that.

61
00:56:22.786 --> 00:56:25.786
It sounds very bizarre, but I want to make something clear today.

62
00:56:25.786 --> 00:56:27.786
We will soon see where this is going.

63
00:56:27.786 --> 00:56:33.786
But if I reflect this text against my own life, against your lives,

64
00:56:33.786 --> 00:56:37.786
then I think we can rightly say that

65
00:56:37.786 --> 00:56:39.786
I have a few points to work on.

66
00:56:39.786 --> 00:56:43.786
Or is there anyone who can say check, check, check.

67
00:56:43.786 --> 00:56:45.786
It's all in order. I don't think so.

68
00:56:47.786 --> 00:56:50.786
There are people who will probably say that

69
00:56:50.786 --> 00:56:52.786
and I can perfectly imagine that,

70
00:56:52.786 --> 00:56:56.786
who, growing up in a family,

71
00:56:56.786 --> 00:56:59.786
feel like they can never reach that.

72
00:56:59.786 --> 00:57:02.786
You have people who are so insecure about themselves and who say,

73
00:57:02.786 --> 00:57:06.786
yes, no, I will never succeed.

74
00:57:07.786 --> 00:57:09.786
There are some who might say,

75
00:57:09.786 --> 00:57:14.786
yes, okay, I can see that happening, but what if that other person would just change.

76
00:57:15.786 --> 00:57:18.786
That could also be the case, that such people are here.

77
00:57:19.786 --> 00:57:23.786
And actually, we often have excuses.

78
00:57:23.786 --> 00:57:29.786
And the text that is here is really meant to confront.

79
00:57:30.786 --> 00:57:32.786
It also comes from Corinthians.

80
00:57:32.786 --> 00:57:35.786
I don't know if you know the story of the congregation of Corinth.

81
00:57:35.786 --> 00:57:37.786
I'm not going to elaborate too much on that,

82
00:57:37.786 --> 00:57:40.786
but there was a congregation that had some difficulties.

83
00:57:40.786 --> 00:57:42.786
There were many voices in that congregation.

84
00:57:42.786 --> 00:57:45.786
There were many teachers and the people formed groups.

85
00:57:45.786 --> 00:57:47.786
There was division.

86
00:57:48.786 --> 00:57:50.786
I'm not a hundred percent sure anymore.

87
00:57:50.786 --> 00:57:53.786
I might be a little bit wrong. I should have prepared it better.

88
00:57:53.786 --> 00:57:58.786
But that was actually a situation where a son-in-law was dealing with his mother-in-law.

89
00:57:58.786 --> 00:58:02.786
Well, in any case, things that make us think that

90
00:58:02.786 --> 00:58:04.786
wow, that congregation was indeed in difficulties.

91
00:58:04.786 --> 00:58:08.786
And at that moment, Paul writes this to that congregation.

92
00:58:08.786 --> 00:58:14.786
So I think this can be perfectly used today in the congregation that we are.

93
00:58:15.786 --> 00:58:19.786
We also have difficulties. We are also people with difficulties.

94
00:58:20.786 --> 00:58:23.786
So don't think that it was different back then than it is now.

95
00:58:23.786 --> 00:58:28.786
And you know what? If you read this passage in chapter 12 and chapter 14,

96
00:58:28.786 --> 00:58:33.786
then right in the middle of the text about spiritual gifts,

97
00:58:33.786 --> 00:58:36.786
many people use this text as very romantic of course.

98
00:58:36.786 --> 00:58:38.786
At a wedding.

99
00:58:38.786 --> 00:58:41.786
Love is patient, kind.

100
00:58:41.786 --> 00:58:43.786
Yes, that's true.

101
00:58:43.786 --> 00:58:45.786
But you have work to do.

102
00:58:45.786 --> 00:58:49.786
But strictly speaking, in the context where it stands here,

103
00:58:49.786 --> 00:58:52.786
it's like, look, you can have spiritual gifts.

104
00:58:52.786 --> 00:58:54.786
And Tim has spoken about that.

105
00:58:54.786 --> 00:58:58.786
And do you know what is so important to know about those spiritual gifts?

106
00:58:58.786 --> 00:59:00.786
God gives those.

107
00:59:00.786 --> 00:59:02.786
I haven't earned anything there.

108
00:59:02.786 --> 00:59:05.786
Actually, speaking here.

109
00:59:05.786 --> 00:59:09.786
And the words I say, that has been given to me.

110
00:59:09.786 --> 00:59:13.786
And if I didn't do it with love,

111
00:59:13.786 --> 00:59:16.786
then it would mean nothing.

112
00:59:16.786 --> 00:59:20.786
And I must therefore be very vigilant to keep that love in mind.

113
00:59:20.786 --> 00:59:22.786
That's why I started by saying,

114
00:59:22.786 --> 00:59:25.786
I really enjoy putting a face to your names,

115
00:59:25.786 --> 00:59:28.786
so that I know for whom I can pray.

116
00:59:28.786 --> 00:59:34.786
Now, the text that follows, John 13, verses 34 and 35,

117
00:59:34.786 --> 00:59:39.786
gives us insight into who has commanded us that.

118
00:59:39.786 --> 00:59:43.786
And we all know, of course, Jesus speaks about that and commands us that.

119
00:59:43.786 --> 00:59:47.786
And he also simultaneously says to whom we should take as an example.

120
00:59:47.786 --> 00:59:52.786
And it says, I give you a new command.

121
00:59:52.786 --> 00:59:54.786
So that is about having to.

122
00:59:54.786 --> 00:59:56.786
Yes? Have to.

123
00:59:56.786 --> 01:00:00.786
Don't we like to hear in our society today that we have to do something?

124
01:00:00.786 --> 01:00:02.786
But I give you a new law.

125
01:00:02.786 --> 01:00:06.786
Not as much as I love you.

126
01:00:06.786 --> 01:00:10.786
If you love one another a lot, everyone will be able to see

127
01:00:10.786 --> 01:00:13.786
that you are my disciples.

128
01:00:13.786 --> 01:00:15.786
And that is ultimately what it is all about.

129
01:00:15.786 --> 01:00:17.786
And I can also refer to this text again.

130
01:00:17.786 --> 01:00:19.786
And there are several parts from this text,

131
01:00:19.786 --> 01:00:22.786
but I want to pick out one specific thing.

132
01:00:22.786 --> 01:00:25.786
And now you might think, he has already read two texts

133
01:00:25.786 --> 01:00:28.786
and he is not going to use them. But it will come.

134
01:00:28.786 --> 01:00:31.786
New law, a command, you have to do it.

135
01:00:31.786 --> 01:00:35.786
Love one another, so that everyone sees that you are my disciples.

136
01:00:35.786 --> 01:00:38.786
God will become known through this.

137
01:00:38.786 --> 01:00:41.786
That is His intention with that love for one another.

138
01:00:41.786 --> 01:00:44.786
So it is actually about a piece of evangelism.

139
01:00:44.786 --> 01:00:47.786
If you sometimes wonder, I don't know if you find that difficult.

140
01:00:47.786 --> 01:00:50.786
I find it difficult to evangelize.

141
01:00:50.786 --> 01:00:52.786
To tell people who God is.

142
01:00:52.786 --> 01:00:54.786
Even though I love him immensely.

143
01:00:54.786 --> 01:00:56.786
I actually sometimes get a bit fed up

144
01:00:56.786 --> 01:00:59.786
with all those arguments that people throw against it

145
01:00:59.786 --> 01:01:02.786
to tell about who He is.

146
01:01:02.786 --> 01:01:04.786
And then God actually says here,

147
01:01:04.786 --> 01:01:06.786
if you start to do and love one another,

148
01:01:06.786 --> 01:01:09.786
then people will see that you are my disciples.

149
01:01:09.786 --> 01:01:12.786
So it can also be partly without words.

150
01:01:12.786 --> 01:01:15.786
But never give up doing that.

151
01:01:15.786 --> 01:01:18.786
But today I actually want to pause

152
01:01:18.786 --> 01:01:22.786
especially when I love you just as much as you love one another

153
01:01:22.786 --> 01:01:25.786
as I love you.

154
01:01:25.786 --> 01:01:27.786
And that is exactly what today is about.

155
01:01:27.786 --> 01:01:29.786
God is love.

156
01:01:29.786 --> 01:01:32.786
And God provides in His love.

157
01:01:32.786 --> 01:01:34.786
I really want to...

158
01:01:34.786 --> 01:01:36.786
Love has so many aspects.

159
01:01:36.786 --> 01:01:39.786
But I really want to talk today about the love

160
01:01:39.786 --> 01:01:42.786
that God has for us.

161
01:01:42.786 --> 01:01:46.786
And we have already sung about it a few times today.

162
01:01:46.786 --> 01:01:48.786
And I am going to tell a few things about it,

163
01:01:48.786 --> 01:01:51.786
about that love for God, from us.

164
01:01:51.786 --> 01:01:54.786
How important it is to grasp that.

165
01:01:54.786 --> 01:01:56.786
And it is important to place that in this church.

166
01:01:56.786 --> 01:01:58.786
In every church in our lives.

167
01:01:58.786 --> 01:02:01.786
And don't think now, men, oh, love, it's going to get cheesy again.

168
01:02:01.786 --> 01:02:03.786
Or women, oh, it's going to be something romantic.

169
01:02:03.786 --> 01:02:05.786
Those are the...

170
01:02:05.786 --> 01:02:08.786
That is the love that we as humans fill in.

171
01:02:08.786 --> 01:02:10.786
It is really about the love of God.

172
01:02:10.786 --> 01:02:12.786
And that Dutch word for love,

173
01:02:12.786 --> 01:02:14.786
has actually become a container concept.

174
01:02:14.786 --> 01:02:16.786
I don't know if you know what a container concept is,

175
01:02:16.786 --> 01:02:19.786
everything is actually thrown into it.

176
01:02:19.786 --> 01:02:22.786
The world, and the world, we mean by that the people

177
01:02:22.786 --> 01:02:25.786
who are not believers, what they understand by love.

178
01:02:26.786 --> 01:02:28.786
That is really not what God intended.

179
01:02:28.786 --> 01:02:30.786
So I want to make that very clear,

180
01:02:30.786 --> 01:02:33.786
of everything that is said in this world,

181
01:02:33.786 --> 01:02:36.786
of what love is, it is not.

182
01:02:37.786 --> 01:02:40.786
What the Bible says about love, that is it.

183
01:02:40.786 --> 01:02:42.786
Let us be clear about that.

184
01:02:42.786 --> 01:02:45.786
And where does it come from, when you start reading in the Bible,

185
01:02:45.786 --> 01:02:47.786
the Bible is written in Greek.

186
01:02:48.786 --> 01:02:52.786
And the word that, yes,

187
01:02:52.786 --> 01:02:56.786
the love of God indicates in Greek is agape.

188
01:02:56.786 --> 01:02:59.786
And I think we have heard that before,

189
01:02:59.786 --> 01:03:01.786
especially if you have been in the church longer.

190
01:03:01.786 --> 01:03:04.786
And I actually looked into that once,

191
01:03:04.786 --> 01:03:07.786
what does that mean, this agape?

192
01:03:07.786 --> 01:03:10.786
And that is exactly what that love of God means.

193
01:03:10.786 --> 01:03:13.786
It is an exceptional love.

194
01:03:13.786 --> 01:03:16.786
It is a love that is determined

195
01:03:16.786 --> 01:03:19.786
to be devoted to someone.

196
01:03:20.786 --> 01:03:22.786
Should I repeat that?

197
01:03:23.786 --> 01:03:25.786
I will repeat that.

198
01:03:25.786 --> 01:03:28.786
It is a love that is determined

199
01:03:28.786 --> 01:03:32.786
to be devoted to someone else.

200
01:03:34.786 --> 01:03:37.786
It is a love that pays attention to people.

201
01:03:37.786 --> 01:03:42.786
without there being physical attraction or agreement, affection.

202
01:03:43.786 --> 01:03:47.786
And do you know what is even so? That love is not mutual.

203
01:03:48.786 --> 01:03:52.786
Then when I wanted to start with this word,

204
01:03:52.786 --> 01:03:55.786
then I thought, you have something like...

205
01:03:56.786 --> 01:03:59.786
Yes, now I've lost it, but in any case something that is guaranteed,

206
01:03:59.786 --> 01:04:01.786
or something like mutual consent.

207
01:04:01.786 --> 01:04:06.786
But you can refuse the love of God.

208
01:04:06.786 --> 01:04:08.786
You can do that.

209
01:04:08.786 --> 01:04:14.786
But that does not detract from His love for you at all.

210
01:04:18.786 --> 01:04:20.786
It is a love that departs,

211
01:04:20.786 --> 01:04:23.786
so what I just said, from the will to love someone,

212
01:04:23.786 --> 01:04:27.786
without that meaning that the person responds to this love.

213
01:04:27.786 --> 01:04:31.786
And when I speak in this sermon today about the love of God,

214
01:04:31.786 --> 01:04:35.786
I am talking about that agape love.

215
01:04:36.786 --> 01:04:43.786
That love that is determined, that does not change, that does not alter.

216
01:04:44.786 --> 01:04:47.786
I find it funny that I have written it down here now.

217
01:04:47.786 --> 01:04:49.786
It is a bit special that you find yourself funny,

218
01:04:49.786 --> 01:04:51.786
but let's not talk about that today.

219
01:04:51.786 --> 01:04:52.786
No, it is not that special.

220
01:04:52.786 --> 01:04:54.786
Thank you, Caroline.

221
01:04:54.786 --> 01:04:59.786
God does not love us because we are so attractive or so great.

222
01:04:59.786 --> 01:05:01.786
These are all human interpretations of love.

223
01:05:01.786 --> 01:05:02.786
We often think that way.

224
01:05:02.786 --> 01:05:04.786
We must put our best foot forward.

225
01:05:04.786 --> 01:05:06.786
We must do a lot of work.

226
01:05:06.786 --> 01:05:09.786
We must look impeccable.

227
01:05:09.786 --> 01:05:12.786
But that is actually something we fill in ourselves.

228
01:05:12.786 --> 01:05:15.786
And that is not how you should approach God.

229
01:05:15.786 --> 01:05:18.786
He loves you just as you are.

230
01:05:18.786 --> 01:05:22.786
And I had actually written this down, and I will be honest about it,

231
01:05:22.786 --> 01:05:25.786
because it is from a study Bible and I still want to read it,

232
01:05:25.786 --> 01:05:27.786
because it was something beautiful.

233
01:05:27.786 --> 01:05:31.786
Love has God as its ultimate source.

234
01:05:32.786 --> 01:05:34.786
It comes from Him.

235
01:05:36.786 --> 01:05:39.786
That a believer loves others,

236
01:05:40.786 --> 01:05:45.786
suggests that he or she has a relationship with God.

237
01:05:47.786 --> 01:05:52.786
A believer who loves others has a relationship with God, it says there.

238
01:05:54.786 --> 01:06:00.786
If someone loves God, he will also love what God loves.

239
01:06:01.786 --> 01:06:03.786
Also yourself.

240
01:06:03.786 --> 01:06:07.786
And in this context, that especially means other believers.

241
01:06:07.786 --> 01:06:08.786
So it is written in the Bible.

242
01:06:08.786 --> 01:06:14.786
Another lover is not the cause, but the result of a regeneration.

243
01:06:14.786 --> 01:06:17.786
That is the result of a choice you make for God.

244
01:06:18.786 --> 01:06:20.786
And as a member of the heavenly family,

245
01:06:20.786 --> 01:06:24.786
the believer reflects this family trait of love.

246
01:06:25.786 --> 01:06:27.786
It belongs to you.

247
01:06:27.786 --> 01:06:30.786
You simply cannot do without that love.

248
01:06:30.786 --> 01:06:35.786
If you understand the love God has for you, you cannot help but express it.

249
01:06:35.786 --> 01:06:37.786
It is a family trait.

250
01:06:37.786 --> 01:06:40.786
We are all family to each other, do you know that?

251
01:06:40.786 --> 01:06:42.786
All of us.

252
01:06:42.786 --> 01:06:48.786
It is even impossible to be a recipient of God's love and to enter into a relationship with Him,

253
01:06:48.786 --> 01:06:53.786
without then showing that same love to others.

254
01:06:53.786 --> 01:06:57.786
Especially, but not exclusively, to other Christians.

255
01:06:58.786 --> 01:07:00.786
That is what the Bible says about it.

256
01:07:01.786 --> 01:07:04.786
Beautiful, He is the source, the ultimate source of love.

257
01:07:04.786 --> 01:07:08.786
And now you might say, I want to mention it very briefly,

258
01:07:08.786 --> 01:07:13.786
that love towards others has to do with service.

259
01:07:14.786 --> 01:07:17.786
It has to do with doing good for others.

260
01:07:18.786 --> 01:07:23.786
But also be alert that it does not go too far.

261
01:07:23.786 --> 01:07:27.786
You also need wisdom about what to do for someone else.

262
01:07:28.786 --> 01:07:34.786
It often happens, and certainly we as Christians, and I have often struggled with this,

263
01:07:34.786 --> 01:07:37.786
that you always have to be good to everyone.

264
01:07:37.786 --> 01:07:39.786
And that can be abused.

265
01:07:39.786 --> 01:07:42.786
I just want to address that here.

266
01:07:42.786 --> 01:07:47.786
Being of service does not mean that you always have to do exactly what the other says.

267
01:07:47.786 --> 01:07:51.786
It mainly means that you have to do what is right, what God has asked you to do.

268
01:07:51.786 --> 01:07:53.786
That is what it actually means.

269
01:07:54.786 --> 01:07:58.786
Throughout the whole Bible, we see God's character and love for humanity.

270
01:07:58.786 --> 01:08:03.786
And God's love can be found in every book of the Bible.

271
01:08:04.786 --> 01:08:07.786
And some verses specifically say that God is love.

272
01:08:07.786 --> 01:08:09.786
Actually, why does God do that so often?

273
01:08:09.786 --> 01:08:14.786
Why in every book of the Bible and very explicitly in certain verses?

274
01:08:14.786 --> 01:08:17.786
He does not want us to have doubts about it.

275
01:08:17.786 --> 01:08:20.786
He does not want us to doubt His love for us.

276
01:08:21.786 --> 01:08:27.786
The Bible says that He loves us, because He loves us.

277
01:08:27.786 --> 01:08:30.786
I can't really say it better than that.

278
01:08:30.786 --> 01:08:34.786
He loves us simply because that is how it is.

279
01:08:35.786 --> 01:08:38.786
I could conclude now, I think.

280
01:08:38.786 --> 01:08:41.786
But I still have a while.

281
01:08:41.786 --> 01:08:44.786
But He loves us because it is so ordinary.

282
01:08:44.786 --> 01:08:48.786
I know that is difficult for us as humans to accept.

283
01:08:48.786 --> 01:08:53.786
If you look at how often we are even in relationships.

284
01:08:53.786 --> 01:08:58.786
We are not used to taking something without having to give something in return.

285
01:08:58.786 --> 01:09:00.786
But that is exactly what God means.

286
01:09:00.786 --> 01:09:02.786
That is what He wants.

287
01:09:02.786 --> 01:09:04.786
He says from here.

288
01:09:05.786 --> 01:09:08.786
Yes, but do I have to do something?

289
01:09:08.786 --> 01:09:10.786
No, take.

290
01:09:10.786 --> 01:09:12.786
That is what you must do.

291
01:09:12.786 --> 01:09:14.786
1 John 4, verse 16.

292
01:09:14.786 --> 01:09:19.786
I want to quote a text that literally states that God is love.

293
01:09:19.786 --> 01:09:23.786
We have seen and believed that God loves us very much.

294
01:09:23.786 --> 01:09:25.786
God is love.

295
01:09:25.786 --> 01:09:27.786
That is literally stated in the Bible.

296
01:09:27.786 --> 01:09:32.786
And if you love each other just like God loves you, you remain in God and God remains in you.

297
01:09:32.786 --> 01:09:36.786
The love that God has for us is sacrificial.

298
01:09:36.786 --> 01:09:41.786
It is a love that continues to care for the other, no matter the cost.

299
01:09:41.786 --> 01:09:43.786
That is the love of God for us.

300
01:09:43.786 --> 01:09:45.786
That is the love that God has for us.

301
01:09:45.786 --> 01:09:51.786
And despite the fact that we make mistakes and are sinful, God still loves us.

302
01:09:51.786 --> 01:09:55.786
There is no way to get a pin between it.

303
01:09:55.786 --> 01:09:59.786
But that is the advantage, of course, if you stand for this.

304
01:09:59.786 --> 01:10:02.786
No one can start to argue with you.

305
01:10:02.786 --> 01:10:05.786
You can just say, that's how it is.

306
01:10:05.786 --> 01:10:09.786
You might think that, but you will really keep insisting.

307
01:10:09.786 --> 01:10:10.786
God is love.

308
01:10:10.786 --> 01:10:17.786
You can spend a long time pondering and trying to grasp that, trying to understand it.

309
01:10:17.786 --> 01:10:19.786
But it is just so.

310
01:10:19.786 --> 01:10:22.786
It is just so.

311
01:10:22.786 --> 01:10:25.786
And you know what, if you take that leap.

312
01:10:25.786 --> 01:10:27.786
Because that is also it.

313
01:10:27.786 --> 01:10:31.786
If you really take the leap to say, I accept that love of God for me.

314
01:10:31.786 --> 01:10:34.786
That is a leap into the deep.

315
01:10:34.786 --> 01:10:38.786
You really cannot assess that in advance.

316
01:10:38.786 --> 01:10:42.786
It is just, you become convinced of that love of His for us.

317
01:10:42.786 --> 01:10:44.786
You jump into that water.

318
01:10:44.786 --> 01:10:47.786
You are completely surrounded by that water.

319
01:10:47.786 --> 01:10:50.786
Just as you are surrounded by Him.

320
01:10:50.786 --> 01:10:53.786
And then you think, oh dear, what is happening now?

321
01:10:53.786 --> 01:10:56.786
He is going to teach you how to swim.

322
01:10:56.786 --> 01:11:01.786
He is going to teach you how to breathe underwater.

323
01:11:01.786 --> 01:11:05.786
He is going to take you to places underwater where you have never been before.

324
01:11:05.786 --> 01:11:08.786
And there he is going to help you.

325
01:11:08.786 --> 01:11:10.786
Do you know that God loves us?

326
01:11:10.786 --> 01:11:13.786
And I want to emphasize that he provides for that love.

327
01:11:13.786 --> 01:11:15.786
And do you know what is also so beautiful about that love?

328
01:11:15.786 --> 01:11:17.786
It is unconditional, that love.

329
01:11:17.786 --> 01:11:19.786
And it never stops.

330
01:11:19.786 --> 01:11:22.786
In English, they say, relentless.

331
01:11:22.786 --> 01:11:28.786
Relentless. He will never stop fully embracing you.

332
01:11:28.786 --> 01:11:30.786
Understand that well?

333
01:11:30.786 --> 01:11:33.786
If you sometimes think that...

334
01:11:33.786 --> 01:11:37.786
And I think the testimonies are enough from people who have been Christians for a longer time.

335
01:11:37.786 --> 01:11:39.786
It is sometimes difficult.

336
01:11:39.786 --> 01:11:46.786
But that is simply because we struggle against what God wants for us.

337
01:11:46.786 --> 01:11:49.786
In his love, he is much wiser than we are.

338
01:11:49.786 --> 01:11:52.786
And he wants to get us to a certain place.

339
01:11:52.786 --> 01:11:57.786
And every time we think, yes but no, that is going to hurt.

340
01:11:57.786 --> 01:11:59.786
It is going to hurt.

341
01:11:59.786 --> 01:12:01.786
And then you might think, it's going to hurt.

342
01:12:01.786 --> 01:12:03.786
But He wants to get us there.

343
01:12:03.786 --> 01:12:05.786
And surrender yourself.

344
01:12:05.786 --> 01:12:08.786
He will teach you to swim, He will teach you to breathe underwater.

345
01:12:08.786 --> 01:12:12.786
And when you start to think, I don't know, just where that text is.

346
01:12:12.786 --> 01:12:16.786
Nothing will be able to separate us from the love of God.

347
01:12:16.786 --> 01:12:19.786
We know that text well, I don't know exactly where it is.

348
01:12:19.786 --> 01:12:23.786
That means exactly what we are talking about here.

349
01:12:23.786 --> 01:12:25.786
It is God's love for us.

350
01:12:25.786 --> 01:12:26.786
That will never stop.

351
01:12:26.786 --> 01:12:29.786
God will never allow us to be separated from His love.

352
01:12:29.786 --> 01:12:32.786
But I can tell you, everything will try to separate you from that love.

353
01:12:35.786 --> 01:12:38.786
Literally, everything will try to separate you from His love.

354
01:12:38.786 --> 01:12:41.786
And God's side is firm.

355
01:12:42.786 --> 01:12:44.786
It is firm, unshakeable.

356
01:12:44.786 --> 01:12:52.786
I don't know if you remember from last week, unless you only caught the Moutias Miel from the sermon.

357
01:12:52.786 --> 01:12:56.786
But Tim talked about the Holy Spirit and at one point he used an image.

358
01:12:56.786 --> 01:13:01.786
And that was a dove as a symbol for the Holy Spirit and how sensitive the Holy Spirit is.

359
01:13:01.786 --> 01:13:05.786
If you clap or allow something in your life, that Holy Spirit is gone.

360
01:13:05.786 --> 01:13:08.786
Well, that love of God is just the opposite.

361
01:13:08.786 --> 01:13:16.786
You can stomp, you can clap, you can shout, you can ignore it, you can spit it out.

362
01:13:16.786 --> 01:13:18.786
But His love stands firm.

363
01:13:18.786 --> 01:13:22.786
And will never waver and is unconditional and will never cease.

364
01:13:23.786 --> 01:13:27.786
That is why it is so important to teach about it.

365
01:13:28.786 --> 01:13:31.786
Because if you think, that love is no longer for me.

366
01:13:32.786 --> 01:13:34.786
The love of God remains.

367
01:13:34.786 --> 01:13:36.786
You can do what you want.

368
01:13:36.786 --> 01:13:38.786
It stays.

369
01:13:44.786 --> 01:13:47.786
The love of God is steadfast and unchanging.

370
01:13:48.786 --> 01:13:51.786
And we all know, and we have sung about it very often today,

371
01:13:51.786 --> 01:13:57.786
that Jesus is the ultimate act of love from God towards us.

372
01:13:57.786 --> 01:14:02.786
And it is also exactly the way to the Father, to God.

373
01:14:03.786 --> 01:14:08.786
And if you do not know that love personally, then I would say, you can always step in.

374
01:14:09.786 --> 01:14:11.786
Maybe a strange term, step in.

375
01:14:11.786 --> 01:14:15.786
But that simply means, I can surrender myself to God.

376
01:14:15.786 --> 01:14:17.786
And I can start to accept that love.

377
01:14:17.786 --> 01:14:19.786
Because that is what He wants, ultimately.

378
01:14:22.786 --> 01:14:25.786
I can also immediately give the advice that it is important

379
01:14:25.786 --> 01:14:29.786
and that it becomes a challenge to continue to cherish that love of God.

380
01:14:30.786 --> 01:14:32.786
And never to forget.

381
01:14:33.786 --> 01:14:35.786
Pray actively.

382
01:14:35.786 --> 01:14:38.786
And by that I mean, consciously.

383
01:14:39.786 --> 01:14:45.786
That this love, and all aspects of this love, may be revealed.

384
01:14:46.786 --> 01:14:49.786
In your personal life, but also towards the people you meet.

385
01:14:49.786 --> 01:14:51.786
And also particularly in the church.

386
01:14:51.786 --> 01:14:53.786
Pray actively for that.

387
01:14:53.786 --> 01:14:56.786
That is an instrument we have been given, to pray.

388
01:15:02.786 --> 01:15:05.786
If you have in mind the love of God for you,

389
01:15:06.786 --> 01:15:08.786
and the fact that it never changes,

390
01:15:08.786 --> 01:15:14.786
then you are actually able to carry out what is stated in Matthew 22, verses 37 to 39.

391
01:15:16.786 --> 01:15:24.786
He said to them, love your Lord, God, with all your heart, with all your soul, and with all your mind.

392
01:15:24.786 --> 01:15:27.786
This is the first and greatest commandment.

393
01:15:27.786 --> 01:15:29.786
Again, that commandment.

394
01:15:30.786 --> 01:15:35.786
It sounds strange, we are in a society where nothing is required and everything is allowed.

395
01:15:36.786 --> 01:15:40.786
But still, we see here two things where God tells us, do that now.

396
01:15:42.786 --> 01:15:44.786
Just do that.

397
01:15:44.786 --> 01:15:50.786
If you apply that, and you start doing it, then something good will work out in your life.

398
01:15:51.786 --> 01:15:56.786
That is a commandment, and the commandments of God are pure and holy and clean.

399
01:15:57.786 --> 01:16:00.786
The second, as important as the first, is this.

400
01:16:00.786 --> 01:16:04.786
Love your brothers and sisters as much as yourself.

401
01:16:06.786 --> 01:16:12.786
Only when we love the church of God, does the power of God become available and visible.

402
01:16:12.786 --> 01:16:14.786
Invisible and useful.

403
01:16:15.786 --> 01:16:17.786
It may sound strange when I use the word useful.

404
01:16:18.786 --> 01:16:25.786
In principle, if there is no unity, then we can keep praying.

405
01:16:25.786 --> 01:16:29.786
And don't get me wrong, what I actually want to say here is,

406
01:16:29.786 --> 01:16:35.786
if you have something against someone else for yourself,

407
01:16:36.786 --> 01:16:41.786
or if it's not for me, then you miss His love.

408
01:16:42.786 --> 01:16:45.786
And that is so important, it binds everything together.

409
01:16:46.786 --> 01:16:50.786
I already said it earlier, spiritual gifts without love mean nothing after all.

410
01:16:51.786 --> 01:16:55.786
We need that, if we do not hold that in our minds.

411
01:16:56.786 --> 01:16:59.786
We ourselves are not capable of having love for each other or for unbelievers.

412
01:16:59.786 --> 01:17:02.786
And I am talking about agape love, I already mentioned that at the beginning,

413
01:17:02.786 --> 01:17:04.786
it is important to keep that in mind.

414
01:17:04.786 --> 01:17:07.786
An exceptional love that expects nothing in return.

415
01:17:08.786 --> 01:17:13.786
A determined choice to have love.

416
01:17:15.786 --> 01:17:19.786
If you do not understand that God made that choice for you,

417
01:17:19.786 --> 01:17:21.786
then you cannot share that either.

418
01:17:22.786 --> 01:17:26.786
So you must be determined to have love back for Him.

419
01:17:27.786 --> 01:17:30.786
That is why it is important to make a choice for Him.

420
01:17:31.786 --> 01:17:36.786
For it is not just that we say that every week, to choose Jesus, choose Him.

421
01:17:36.786 --> 01:17:38.786
Respond to his love.

422
01:17:41.786 --> 01:17:46.786
And do you know what it is, when you start to choose, you really know what God means to you,

423
01:17:46.786 --> 01:17:49.786
and we learn to love God as well.

424
01:17:49.786 --> 01:17:54.786
And I want to emphasize again that it is a process that starts with yourself.

425
01:17:55.786 --> 01:17:59.786
At the beginning, I said, maybe there are people here who say,

426
01:17:59.786 --> 01:18:02.786
if that one would just stop being so annoying,

427
01:18:02.786 --> 01:18:05.786
and constantly bothering me,

428
01:18:05.786 --> 01:18:09.786
then I can start to distribute that love. That is not what the Bible says.

429
01:18:11.786 --> 01:18:17.786
Can we please stop making the responsibility to love ourselves,

430
01:18:17.786 --> 01:18:19.786
depend on other people?

431
01:18:22.786 --> 01:18:25.786
Do you know what the danger is if you do that?

432
01:18:25.786 --> 01:18:29.786
The risk is that his love will pass you by.

433
01:18:31.786 --> 01:18:34.786
That you end up in a situation where it is too late.

434
01:18:36.786 --> 01:18:39.786
And we really do not want to end up there.

435
01:18:42.786 --> 01:18:50.786
His love is ready, never ends, is unconditional, is pure, is holy, is clean.

436
01:18:50.786 --> 01:18:58.786
And why do I emphasize that there is actually no risk in surrendering to him?

437
01:18:58.786 --> 01:19:01.786
Then only that you will be completely surrounded by his love,

438
01:19:01.786 --> 01:19:05.786
and lead a life that you never thought possible.

439
01:19:06.786 --> 01:19:12.786
I dare to say that a lack of love for God, for yourself, and for others,

440
01:19:12.786 --> 01:19:15.786
is downright dangerous for us.

441
01:19:15.786 --> 01:19:17.786
You don't want that.

442
01:19:17.786 --> 01:19:21.786
Just imagine living a life without love.

443
01:19:21.786 --> 01:19:26.786
When you talk to people, believers and non-believers,

444
01:19:26.786 --> 01:19:30.786
who have lacked love in their upbringing,

445
01:19:31.786 --> 01:19:36.786
they spend their whole lives seeking confirmation of that love.

446
01:19:36.786 --> 01:19:41.786
And they try to find it in all sorts of ways.

447
01:19:42.786 --> 01:19:48.786
And I can tell you that if you seek it somewhere other than in God Himself,

448
01:19:48.786 --> 01:19:51.786
it will only cause you more pain.

449
01:19:51.786 --> 01:19:55.786
It will cause even more problems.

450
01:19:55.786 --> 01:19:57.786
So run to Him.

451
01:19:58.786 --> 01:20:03.786
And when we want to reach the people around us, our family, our friends, our acquaintances,

452
01:20:03.786 --> 01:20:07.786
we need to start breathing out that love.

453
01:20:07.786 --> 01:20:12.786
It must become an integral part of our being, of who we are.

454
01:20:12.786 --> 01:20:15.786
And He will help you with that.

455
01:20:15.786 --> 01:20:18.786
You know what? No one benefits from religion.

456
01:20:18.786 --> 01:20:21.786
We do benefit from a living God,

457
01:20:21.786 --> 01:20:27.786
who has also chosen to love us and uses us to carry that love.

458
01:20:28.786 --> 01:20:31.786
Just think of that verse I read from John.

459
01:20:31.786 --> 01:20:36.786
If you love one another, everyone will see that you are my disciples.

460
01:20:37.786 --> 01:20:41.786
Because that is ultimately what God is about. Do you know that?

461
01:20:42.786 --> 01:20:45.786
That he becomes visible.

462
01:20:45.786 --> 01:20:48.786
That he becomes known.

463
01:20:49.786 --> 01:20:54.786
A church is not there to show how talented you are.

464
01:20:54.786 --> 01:21:01.786
A church is not there as a forum to show how many good works you have.

465
01:21:01.786 --> 01:21:06.786
A church is there to show that we have a living God,

466
01:21:06.786 --> 01:21:09.786
who loves us and wants to move forward with us.

467
01:21:09.786 --> 01:21:12.786
And who wants to ensure that all those chairs you see empty now,

468
01:21:12.786 --> 01:21:17.786
